From 2c71a49c7da7882599449818bb9dc06eb31958b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 19:09:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 382/638] [AROS] Add native Chromium Workbench icon

Add an AROS-specific 128x128 Chromium tool icon with distinct normal and selected imagery, a reproducible high-resolution RGBA source, and a native Amiga Workbench .info payload. Define a 10 MiB stack and CHROME_ARG ToolTypes for browser defaults plus disabled optional fullscreen, incognito, software-rendering, logging, and URL choices.

AI_PHASE: chromium-workbench-integration
AI_STATUS: native-icon-packaged
ROOT_CAUSE: Hosted Chromium was only launchable as a bare executable without native Workbench identity or configurable launch metadata.
FIX_REASON: Package a real AROS TOOL icon and explicit ToolTypes before validating Workbench startup.
SCOPE: chrome/app/theme/aros
VALIDATION: ilbmtoicon produced a 105378-byte Amiga Workbench tool icon; infoinfo verified 128x128 dimensions, STACK=10485760, normal/selected imagery, and all ToolTypes.
RISK: Workbench argument consumption is committed separately after compile validation.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: working browser window -> native application identity missing -> generate AROS-specific mark -> package with native icon tooling -> verify metadata.
Evidence: test-artifacts/-chromium-browser-renderer-20260728/icon-02-ilbmtoicon.log; test-artifacts/-chromium-browser-renderer-20260728/icon-03-infoinfo.log
Job:
